    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3261" textLabel="MONOMER-3261" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3261" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The vte3 mutant plants have a significant decrease in alpha and gamma-tocopherol content, and an increase of beta and delta-tocopherol content. It provided genetic evidence that the vte3 locus is responsible for the MPBQ methyltransferase activity and is involved in tocopherol biosynthesis. In addition, plastoquinone level is also significantly decreased in the vte3 mutants which indicates that vte3 is also involved in plastoquinone biosynthesis. Vte3 was expressed in E.coli and in-vitro assay demonstrated that it encodes the MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase and the enzyme uses both MPBQ and MSBQ as substrates.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-3261" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="MPBQ/MSBQ methyltransferase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22132, RXN-12804, RXN-3421, RXN-3841" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G63410.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-2341" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="12787252" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightKd" value="37.9" />
      <Property key="MolecularWeightSeq" value="37.9" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_14508009" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3281" textLabel="tocopherol cyclase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3281" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Expressing of the vte1 cDNA in E.coli followed by enzyme assay demonstrated that vte1 encodes a tocopherol cyclase, and that both 2,3-dimethyl-6-phytyl-1,4-benzoquinone (DMPBQ) and 2,3-dimethyl-6-geranylgeranyl-1,4-benzoquinone (DMGBQ) are substrates. When DMGBQ is used as a substrate, gamma-tocotrienol is synthesized. All four forms of tocopherols are absent in the vte1 mutant plants indicates the enzyme also converts 2-methyl-6-phytyl-1,4-benzoquinone to delta-tocopherol. The vte1 encoded protein has a chloroplast transit peptide.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-3281" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-22499, RXN-22500, RXN-3442, RXN-3441" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G32770.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="G-2361" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="12213958" />
