    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-3282" textLabel="MONOMER-3282" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-3282" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Expressing the enzyme in E.coli confirmed its methylation activity with both gamma- and delta-tocopherols. Beta-tocopherol is not a substrate which indicates the enzyme specifically methylates the C-5 position of the aromatic ring. Over expressing in Arabidopsis seeds changed tocopherol composition (increased alpha-tocopherol) but not total content.</Comment>
